From: =?utf-8?b?T3R0byBLZWvDpGzDpGluZW4=?= <otto@debian.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 13:51:47 +0000
Subject: Handle WITH_LIBWRAP correctly to silence CMake CMP0077 warning

CMake 3.13+ now treats `option()` as a cache variable and warns when a
normal variable of the same name already exists. The MySQL release
configuration was setting `WITH_LIBWRAP` as a normal variable, which
caused the policy warning during configuration.

Promote the assignment to a cache entry so the variable kind matches
what the subsequent `option(WITH_LIBWRAP ...)` command expects.

Now the configure process will fail with a clear error message if
WITH_LIBWRAP=ON is set but the libwrap development libraries are not
installed, making the build requirements explicit and helping users
understand why their configuration is not working as expected.

Fixes warning:

    CMake Warning (dev) at configure.cmake:145 (OPTION):
      Policy CMP0077 is not set: option() honors normal variables.  Run "cmake
      --help-policy CMP0077" for policy details.  Use the cmake_policy command to
      set the policy and suppress this warning.

      For compatibility with older versions of CMake, option is clearing the
      normal variable 'WITH_LIBWRAP'.
    Call Stack (most recent call first):
      CMakeLists.txt:405 (INCLUDE)
---
 cmake/build_configurations/mysql_release.cmake | 2 +-
 configure.cmake                                | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/build_configurations/mysql_release.cmake b/cmake/build_configurations/mysql_release.cmake
index 8c12064..5ada3d5 100644
--- a/cmake/build_configurations/mysql_release.cmake
+++ b/cmake/build_configurations/mysql_release.cmake
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ ELSEIF(RPM)
 ELSEIF(DEB)
   SET(WITH_SSL system CACHE STRING "")
   SET(WITH_ZLIB system CACHE STRING "")
-  SET(WITH_LIBWRAP ON)
+  SET(WITH_LIBWRAP ON CACHE BOOL "Compile with tcp wrappers support")
   SET(HAVE_EMBEDDED_PRIVILEGE_CONTROL ON)
   # On Hurd systems (GNU) there is no auth socket implementation
   IF(NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "GNU")
diff --git a/configure.cmake b/configure.cmake
index 1a0743bb..7693b45 100644
--- a/configure.cmake
+++ b/configure.cmake
@@ -161,6 +161,8 @@ IF(UNIX)
     IF(HAVE_LIBWRAP)
       SET(MYSYS_LIBWRAP_SOURCE  ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/mysys/my_libwrap.c)
       SET(LIBWRAP "wrap")
+    ELSEIF(WITH_LIBWRAP)
+      MESSAGE(FATAL_ERROR "WITH_LIBWRAP is ON but libwrap (tcp wrappers) was not found. Install libwrap0-dev or set WITH_LIBWRAP=OFF")
     ENDIF()
   ENDIF()
   ADD_FEATURE_INFO(LIBWRAP HAVE_LIBWRAP "Support for tcp wrappers")
